{
  "name": "Orders",
  "description": "One row per order, from checkout on the shop website. The website creates it as `awaiting-payment` (PayPal) or `new` (an order request, when the shop takes no online payment), and afterwards changes only its payment fields, and only when PayPal confirms (a capture it made, or a webhook it verified with PayPal): Paid, a payment problem, a refund. Staff move it on: paid → shipped (with the tracking number) → completed, or cancelled. Internal note, reply draft and tracking number are staff-only: the website never reads or writes them. Nobody marks an order paid without PayPal's confirmation, or, for an order request, the owner's word that the money arrived.",
  "position": 2,
  "agentPrompts": [
    {
      "key": "ship-paid-orders",
      "label": {
        "en": "What do I need to ship today?",
        "zh-CN": "今天要发哪些货？"
      },
      "body": "Read the `busa-shop` skill in this folder and follow \"Payments and orders (收款与订单)\", \"Ship a paid order\": list every order in To ship, oldest first, with the address, phone, items and what to pack. When I tell you an order has shipped and give you the tracking number, write it into Tracking number, set the order to shipped and add a dated line to its internal note. Never set an order to paid yourself.",
      "intent": "change"
    },
    {
      "key": "payment-problems",
      "label": {
        "en": "Explain the payment problems",
        "zh-CN": "解释收款问题"
      },
      "body": "Read the `busa-shop` skill in this folder, then for every order that is awaiting payment for more than a day or has a Payment problem, tell me what PayPal reported (Payment log, Payment problem), what it means and what I should check in my PayPal account. Do not change any order, do not refund and do not mark anything paid.",
      "intent": "read-only"
    },
    {
      "key": "handle-new-orders",
      "label": "Handle today's new order requests",
      "body": "Read the `busa-shop` skill in this folder and follow its \"Handle a new order request\" procedure for every order with status `new`: check the items against the product list and stock, write a reply draft for me to send, and tell me what each order needs. Do not email the customer and do not change an order to paid or shipped yourself."
    },
    {
      "key": "orders-waiting",
      "label": "Which orders are waiting on me?",
      "body": "Read the `busa-shop` skill in this folder, then list orders that are still `new`, `confirmed`, `awaiting-payment` or `paid` (not shipped), oldest first, with how long each has been waiting and what the next step is.",
      "intent": "read-only"
    },
    {
      "key": "mark-order-status",
      "label": "Move an order to its next status",
      "body": "Read the `busa-shop` skill in this folder, then change the status of the order I name to the status I give (confirmed, shipped, completed or cancelled) and add a dated line to its internal note saying who asked for the change. Only do this when I tell you the step really happened. Paid is set by PayPal: for an order request paid another way, set it to paid only when I say the money arrived. Never set refunded, and never refund: refunds are made in PayPal."
    }
  ],
